  "lines": [
    {
      "id": "v01",
      "text": "Day one. Rain on the bricks. A knife, a coat, a body under a sheet.",
      "start": 0,
      "duration": 4.54,
      "beat": "b01"
    },
    {
      "id": "v02",
      "text": "By dawn the file was open, and his name was in it.",
      "start": 4.98,
      "duration": 3.48,
      "beat": "b01"
    },
    {
      "id": "v03",
      "text": "Days two and three. He ran through rain; the city kept his face.",
      "start": 8.8,
      "duration": 3.76,
      "beat": "b02"
    },
    {
      "id": "v04",
      "text": "Day four. A train, a tunnel, a ticket on a seat in the dark.",
      "start": 13.14,
      "duration": 3.74,
      "beat": "b02"
    },
    {
      "id": "v05",
      "text": "Days five and six. A rented room, a calendar, a door he did not answer.",
      "start": 17.38,
      "duration": 4.46,
      "beat": "b03"
    },
    {
      "id": "v06",
      "text": "Day seven. The page turned. He counted the hours, not the money.",
      "start": 22.32,
      "duration": 3.84,
      "beat": "b03"
    },
    {
      "id": "v07",
      "text": "Day eight. A checkpoint at the city's edge, and a lamp found his face.",
      "start": 26.16,
      "duration": 4.34,
      "beat": "b04"
    },
    {
      "id": "v08",
      "text": "He turned his collar up and walked through the light without stopping.",
      "start": 31,
      "duration": 3.3,
      "beat": "b04"
    },
    {
      "id": "v09",
      "text": "Day nine. The bridge was wet, and the detective waited at the far end.",
      "start": 34.7,
      "duration": 4.22,
      "beat": "b05"
    },
    {
      "id": "v10",
      "text": "The cuffs closed. The city went on behind him, indifferent.",
      "start": 39.3,
      "duration": 3.4,
      "beat": "b05"
    },
    {
      "id": "v11",
      "text": "Day ten. A cell, a file, a judge, and a sentence read without hurry.",
      "start": 43.16,
      "duration": 4.4,
      "beat": "b06"
    },
    {
      "id": "v12",
      "text": "The gavel fell. The warder took his arm, and the court was empty.",
      "start": 47.9,
      "duration": 3.66,
      "beat": "b06"
    },
    {
      "id": "v13",
      "text": "They brought him back to the same cell, and the calendar still said ten.",
      "start": 51.56,
      "duration": 4,
      "beat": "b07"
    },
    {
      "id": "v14",
      "text": "At dawn they walked him to the yard, where the noose was a shadow.",
      "start": 56.12,
      "duration": 3.42,
      "beat": "b07"
    }
  ],
